      "text": "The bug is `-1 * gate1`. `gate1 = qc.h` binds a method, not a gate, so the multiplication raises a `TypeError`, and the line would do nothing useful even if it ran. Negating a gate is the same as adding a global phase of π, so I replaced that line with `qc.global_phase += np.pi` and added the `numpy` import it needs.\n\n```python\n# FIX: missing numpy import for np.pi -> added import numpy as np, because the global phase fix needs np.pi\nimport numpy as np\nfrom qiskit import QuantumCircuit\n\nqc = QuantumCircuit(2)\nqc.h([0, 1])\n\ngate1 = qc.h\n# FIX: -1 * bound method is invalid (TypeError) and does nothing -> apply a global phase of pi, because multiplying an operator by -1 is exactly e^{i*pi}\nqc.global_phase += np.pi\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
